# osquery-sys prebuilt bundle checksums, schema v1
#
# One line per target triple: TARGET<TAB>SHA256_OF_TAR_ZST (64 lowercase hex
# chars). This file is embedded into the crate itself via include_str! in
# build.rs, so the expected hash for a downloaded prebuilt bundle always
# comes from the same crates.io-published source tree as build.rs's own
# verification logic -- never from the network location serving the bundle
# itself. See build.rs's prebuilt-download path and NEXT_STEPS.md /
# .github/workflows/release.yml for how this file gets populated: the
# release workflow computes each platform's real bundle hash as part of the
# same build that gets uploaded, then commits the result here before
# publishing the GitHub Release.
#
# Empty (no entries below) until the first tagged release's CI run
# populates it -- until then, every target falls back to a from-source
# build with an informational cargo:warning rather than a hard error, since
# "no prebuilt exists yet for this crate version" isn't a release-process
# bug, just the initial/pre-release state.
x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu	db3d9a88c4ab0b246db7705847617716a5cec12e673978ad01d0bd1b4856d5f9
aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu	233f56dd85ca4521ea9007cdb87e6fd7b2b55ddf75697af996c91ce669080ed0
aarch64-apple-darwin	e6b54c6e21bc21fb8e996b08d8b6e6fcafd638a1abe3956268192591a0c3b003
x86_64-pc-windows-msvc	afc94b18c7155473e70cd842193bbae31edbb48239f4db29f97050666f00ad71
